From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: miniperf <miniperf@localhost>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:12:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] i#3544 RISC-V: refill drx_buf buffers on the guard-page
 fault

deduce_buf_ptr() bailed out with an unconditional "Not implemented"
assert on RISCV64, even though the RISC-V arm of the opcode check right
below it was already written. Every drx_buf flavour except
DRX_BUF_CIRCULAR_FAST detects a full buffer by faulting on the read-only
guard page and refilling from the signal handler, and CIRCULAR_FAST's
pointer update is x86-only, so drx_buf was unusable on RISC-V: a client
died at its first buffer wrap.

Drop the assert, and accept sh as a buffer store alongside sb, sw and sd
so a 2-byte drx_buf store is recognised too.
---
 ext/drx/drx_buf.c | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/drx/drx_buf.c b/ext/drx/drx_buf.c
index 5bfcc4fb3..af514f438 100644
--- a/ext/drx/drx_buf.c
+++ b/ext/drx/drx_buf.c
@@ -742,13 +742,10 @@ deduce_buf_ptr(instr_t *instr)
 {
     ushort opcode = (ushort)instr_get_opcode(instr);
 
-#if defined(RISCV64)
-    /* XXX i#3544: Not implemented */
-    DR_ASSERT_MSG(false, "Not implemented");
-#endif
     /* drx_buf will only emit these instructions to store a value */
     if (IF_X86_ELSE(opcode == OP_mov_st,
-                    IF_RISCV64_ELSE(opcode == OP_sb || opcode == OP_sw || opcode == OP_sd,
+                    IF_RISCV64_ELSE(opcode == OP_sb || opcode == OP_sh ||
+                                        opcode == OP_sw || opcode == OP_sd,
                                     opcode == OP_str || opcode == OP_strb ||
                                         opcode == OP_strh))) {
         int i;
